        "raw": "<p>I have a lot of theories about Thiago, and his role in the Sentinels storyline.</p><p>Here is one that I&#39;ve been working on for a while, incorporating some of the recent revelations we&#39;ve seen in the Sentinels Tactics Kickstarter.</p><p>I&#39;ve wondered for a while if Thiago was an orphan (I don&#39;t know if that is confirmed, or was just an idea I had), and speculated about his biological parentage (IE, the Operative being his mother)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thiago was left at a religious orphanage when he was just a baby.&nbsp; Rook city being what it is, there were more than a few orphans, and caring was in precious short supply.&nbsp; As he grew, Thiago became the big brother of the group.&nbsp; He protected the younger kids, not by striking first or starting fights, but by talking with the bullies, finding out what was going on, and playing the role of peacemaker.</p><p>However, Rook city being an unforgiving place, there were always some who only wanted to use violence, and when cornered or given no options, Thiago proved to be adept at fighting.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Flash forward a few years.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Spite is on the prowl, and there is a lot of fear in the orphanage.&nbsp; One of the priests has gone missing, and Thiago (who volunteered at the soup kitchen with the priest) remembered seeing a man in a hoodie talking to him earlier.&nbsp; Thiago has been following the adventures of the heroes around the world, and has started venturing out on his own at night to do what he can against the darkness.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Kind of like the neighborhood watch- just being around in a Legacy shirt staring miscreants down</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">(and there&#39;s something about the way he stares, like he&#39;s not afraid of anything, that makes them think of a terrifying figure from the underworld...).</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Spite sees him, and decides that he&#39;ll make an ideal victim.&nbsp; So he approaches and spends some time gaining the kid&#39;s trust.&nbsp; He senses that the kid is wary, and goes to raid a lab for the night, leaving Thiago for later (the best kills are betrayals of people who trust him, another theory I&rsquo;ve had for a while).&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">The Wraith has been watching from the shadows, and swoops in to rescue the boy.&nbsp;</span></p><p>But seeing her, he wants none of it.&nbsp; He&#39;s willing to be bait. He wants to draw Spite out and get him into position for the Heroes to take him down without collateral damage or innocent bystanders.</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">The Wraith is troubled by this, but Thiago doesn&#39;t back down. Its the right thing to do, and the best way for him to help.&nbsp; She allows it, seeing that Thiago isn&rsquo;t going to back down one bit, and would do it anyway if she tried to prevent it.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">The plan succeeds and Spite goes down (and is imprisoned in the Block), after a terrible fight.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">But the Wraith stays in contact with Thiago afterwards.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Flash forward a few years.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Thiago continues to grow. He&#39;s had a few scrapes on the streets (including a rescue by Mainstay). &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Not that he was afraid. He could have taken them.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Maia Montgomery has been keeping tabs on him, and decides to adopt him. &nbsp;S</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">he hones his skills, both mental and physical. &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">He doesn&#39;t agree with her shadowy ways, and that is the source of a lot of arguments between them.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">However, he does love and admire her, and over the years his arguments start to sound more reasonable to her. &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Maybe it is time for the Wraith to unmask- Several of her enemies already know her identity, and maybe she can do more good bare-faced to the world.</span></p><p>So, she turns over control of Montgomery industries to Thiago, who is proving to be an extremely astute student. She&#39;s bought up Pike&#39;s old businesses, and Rook city is starting to revitalize (though it still has problems!)</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">And Thiago starts standing up for good, justice, and the light as.... <strong>The Chairman.</strong></span></p>",
